_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097162,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTcxNjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/discussion","name":"discussion","color":"ccaaff","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098009,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwMDk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:buildsystem","name":"topic:buildsystem","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2024-10-23T19:21:14Z","updated_at":"2024-11-13T08:48:43Z","closed_at":"2024-11-13T08:33:25Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98470","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98470","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98470.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98470.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"The description of what PR does and the PR itself are smaller than description how this PR done :joy:\r\n\r\nCalling `env[\"vsproj\"]` will result in error if you didn't add the option to variables. I mean if you didn't declare `BoolVariable(\"vsproj\", \"Generate a Visual Studio solution\", False)` which won't declared on non-windows platforms after this PR\r\n\r\nPython has [short circuited bool operators](https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#boolean-operations-and-or-not) so `env[\"vsproj\"]` won't be even evaluated if `\"vsproj\" in env` returned false\r\n\r\nWhy not to use just `\"vsproj\" in env`? :joy: :joy: :joy: Because SCons is very stupidly designed... It was a surprise that `in` operator worked at all. But not as you would expect. :joy: You would expect it to tell you if it contains pair `key, value` with given key. Just like in normal dictionary...\r\n\r\nBut not it will actually tell you if you added \"validator\". I mean this declaration `opts.Add(BoolVariable(\"threads\", \"Enable threading support\", True))`.\r\n\r\nP.S: I am now sick and it is hard to think maybe two previous paragraphs are wrong not by itself but a bit unrelated to this PR","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98470/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98470/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}